00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:13.340
So first of all,
partitioning tables.

00:21:13.340 --> 00:21:17.270
If you are on the Legacy SQL
in BigQuery, very intuitively,

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:19.400
you want to merge the
less frequently used

00:21:19.400 --> 00:21:22.160
small partitions
into bigger ones.

00:21:22.160 --> 00:21:26.180
And if you are already on this
standard SQL these days, what

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:29.530
we actually recommend
you to do is you actually

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:32.490
don't expose the raw
data to end user,

00:21:32.490 --> 00:21:36.170
because that's actually
a white one large piece

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:37.840
of logical partitions.

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:43.130
And instead, you can define the
layer of views for user access

00:21:43.130 --> 00:21:45.560
and using something
called authorized views

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:48.850
to give different user different
access to different portions

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.890
of your partitions.

